---
title: States of an Aggregation Participant (Stuart) - CAS Beacon and SMT Beacon
---

%% One state machine for a DID controller in an Aggregation Cohort.
%% It follows the RECOMMENDED MuSig2 example of the specification (n-of-n),
%% with an optional k-of-n fallback.
%% The update states are in states-did-controller.mmd.

stateDiagram-v2
    state "Not in a cohort" as Out
    state "Enrolled: sent did (CAS) or didIndex (SMT)<br/>and a Schnorr public key" as Enrolled
    state "Check the P2TR Beacon Address:<br/>compute it again from the n public keys<br/>(and k, if the cohort has a k-of-n fallback)" as AddressCheck
    state "Add the CASBeacon or SMTBeacon service<br/>(DID update through the Singleton Beacon)" as AddService
    state "Member of the cohort" as Member {
        state "Wait for an update opportunity" as Wait
        state "Respond (always, also with no update):<br/>CAS: did and updateHash, or no update<br/>SMT: didIndex and leaf value (new nonce)<br/>new MuSig2 nonce" as Respond
        state "Wait for the confirmation request" as WaitRequest
        state "Validate the request:<br/>CAS: own entries and hash of the CAS Announcement<br/>SMT: SMT Proof of each own index against the root" as Validate
        state valid <<choice>>
        state "Send a MuSig2 partial signature" as PartialSign
        state "k-of-n fallback: check the Signal Bytes again,<br/>send a Schnorr signature (script path)" as FallbackSign
        state "Refuse to sign" as Refuse
        state "Wait for the Beacon Signal broadcast" as WaitBroadcast
        state "Keep the round data for the life of the DID:<br/>CAS Announcement, or SMT Proof and nonce,<br/>and the BTCR2 Signed Update (if any)" as Keep

        [*] --> Wait
        Wait --> Respond: update opportunity (pull),<br/>or own update ready (push)
        Respond --> WaitRequest
        WaitRequest --> Wait: round fails (timeout)
        WaitRequest --> Validate: CAS Announcement or SMT Proofs,<br/>Unsigned Beacon Signal, aggregated nonce
        Validate --> valid
        valid --> PartialSign: data matches own submission
        valid --> Refuse: data does not match
        Refuse --> Wait: round fails
        Refuse --> Invalid: k-of-n only, the Beacon Signal goes out<br/>with k signatures and a bad entry
        PartialSign --> WaitBroadcast
        WaitBroadcast --> FallbackSign: fallback request
        FallbackSign --> WaitBroadcast
        WaitBroadcast --> Wait: round fails (never reuse the MuSig2 nonce)
        WaitBroadcast --> Keep: Beacon Signal broadcast
        Keep --> Wait
    }

    state "DID invalid: a resolver cannot get the announced update.<br/>Make a new DID." as Invalid

    [*] --> Out
    Out --> Enrolled: cohort advertised, enroll
    Enrolled --> AddressCheck: Beacon Address and n public keys received
    AddressCheck --> Out: own key missing, or address differs (leave)
    AddressCheck --> AddService: address verified
    AddService --> Member: update settled (minConf)
    Member --> Out: cohort fails, or leave<br/>(remove the beacon service with a DID update)
